Honestly, I don't know for sure, but I'm *quite* sure it would work.
I'd just try...

The larger of the two files (logfile) tracks any game you played by
appending the data record at the end of the file.  The smaller file
(record) contains a list of records sorted by highscore.

Though there is a policy how many entries of some kind may be present
in the record file, I suppose it would not be a problem if there are
"some more" entries in the file than the game would create by itself.
And to my knowledge there is no data dependency to any other sources.

As you observed they are just plain text files.  If you are lucky and
on some Unix system you may just cat the respective files and sort the
record files by the second field and sort logfile by the 10th field to
preserve the chronology. Backup your original record and logfile files
then create the new files

   cat record_1  record_2  | sort +1 -nr > record
   cat logfile_1 logfile_2 | sort +9     > logfile


